<title>SPAIN: PESETA DEBT/INTERBANK CLOSING REPORT.</title>
<headline>PESETA DEBT/INTERBANK CLOSING REPORT.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish government bonds inched higher in the wake of buoyant Bunds on Wednesday after ignoring domestic news for much of the session, dealers said.</p>
<p>&quot;We'll probably continue tracking Bunds this week with little domestic data on the agenda and the market not taking much notice of domestic news anyway,&quot; said one dealer.</p>
<p>Bonos brushed aside lower-than-expected unemployment data. Spain's registered unemployment rate fell to 12.5 percent in July, breaking through the 13 percent barrier for the first time in 16 years.</p>
</text>
